// A **dependency** declares its own `[package] root`, and its intra-package imports lead with that
// rather than with its identity.
//
// The subdirectory `kit/` is a package keyed `kit` here. Its manifest names it
// `noeta-lang/my-toolkit` — a registry coordinate whose halves no `use` could spell — and declares
// `root = "toolkit"`. So `toolkit.noe` writes `use toolkit.text`, which resolves when that package
// is built standalone AND re-roots to `kit` in this build.
//
// This is the pairing that makes a hyphenated identity workable: the coordinate stays a coordinate,
// and every import on both sides of the dependency stays a legal identifier.
// expect: stdout "HI ada"
// expect: exit 0
use kit.toolkit.greet;

echo greet("ada")
